  "summary": "Leaky Skills are instructions for AI agents, typically in SKILL.md files, that cause them to insecurely handle sensitive data like API keys and PII. These skills force agents to pass secrets through LLM context windows, output them in logs, and store them in plaintext, creating exfiltration channels. The report highlights examples from the ClawHub marketplace, such as moltyverse-email and buy-anything, that demonstrate this \"insecurity by design\" pattern.",
